 "geometry_notes": [
  "Low-resolution GIF drawings (475 px wide) read after 4x upscaling; every printed callout legible except the 45 m I-girder vertical chain.",
  "I-girders: top flange has a 30 mm set-back on each side at the top surface (top width = overall - 60) and a 30 mm high full-width lip at the bottom of the flange edge; the set-back to lip transition is modelled as a horizontal step (convention; the GIF shows a short kink).",
  "I-girders: flange underside/overside is two straight tapers meeting at x = +/-200 mm (web half + inner_run); outer taper (60 or 90 high) spans from the flange edge to x=200, inner taper (90 or 120 high) from x=200 to the web.",
  "I45: only the 1400 mm total depth is printed; 270/90/120/440/120/90/270 read by scaling the drawing (0.371 px/mm; each scaled level within 10 mm of these values) and matches the 40/50 m pattern. Provenance estimate.",
  "Hollow girders: 750 mm body, 850 mm bottom ledge (50 mm outstand, 100 mm vertical edge then 50x50 splay); void 370 wide (190 mm walls), top slab 200, vertical void sides 375/475/625, V bottom 75 high; apex 200 mm above soffit closes the printed 850/950/1100 depths.",
  "Compression bars, tendons and ducts are not deducted. No published section properties."
 ],
